-- title:
--   Transcendence of jmatĥ and finiteness of the descended field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. Assume given: a finite set $W$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ (rational affine geometric places at which $j$ takes a supersingular value); an inclusion $\mathrm{hle}$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $A$ with values in that reduced field, whose residue map computes coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$; an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to the Igusa hypotheses (description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ by ratios of Laurent series over $A$ with nonzero reduction of the denominator, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-translates under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, injectivity, and permutation of the family by all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) and the supersingular hypotheses (contraction of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ to $A$ on constants, compatibility of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $R_0$ and with evaluation at $s$ for functions regular wherever $j$ is, invariance under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, and existence of an element of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ whose differences with all constants from $A$ are units); a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ with $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$; the subfield $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ consisting of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$; and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ induced by $\iota$. Then every polynomial over $A_0$ annihilating $\hat\jmath$ in $F_0$ is zero, and $F_0$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield of $F_0$ generated by the image of $A_0$ together with $\hat\jmath$.
--
--   This supplies, for the descended model of the full-level modular curve, the two facts that make $F_0$ a one-variable function field over the constants coming from $A_0$: the modular invariant $\hat\jmath$ is transcendental over those constants, and $F_0$ is a finite extension of the field they generate with $\hat\jmath$. It is used in the construction of the valuation-subring localisations of the chart algebras away from the descent locus.
-- source:
